From: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>
Subject: net: ethernet: mtk_wed: refactor wdma init flow to avoid double init

Backport of MTK SDK patch "refactor wdma init flow to avoid double
init" (999-wed-16-refactor-wdma-init-flow-to-avoid-double-init, recover
the original via `git show eef2a51256:target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/...`).

Re-keys the WDMA RX/TX ring and WED TX/RX ring allocation gates from
"skip alloc if this is a reset" (`!reset`) to "skip alloc if a
descriptor is already allocated" (`!desc`) — allocation becomes
idempotent across repeated resets instead of assuming reset==no-alloc.
CPU_IDX is now only zeroed on `reset` (previously unconditional) in
mtk_wed_wdma_rx_ring_setup(), and mtk_wed_start()'s redundant
pre-loop over dev->rx_wdma[] (which called the same setup function
before the real ring-setup path would anyway) is removed, since ring
setup is no longer reset-gated at the allocation level.

Motivation on this box: wed-03 (CPU_IDX inversion fix) and wed-13
(PSE/WDMA link-down during reset) were built, flashed, and hardware
retested on 2026-07-12 and did NOT clear the mt7915 MCU 0x13ed
FW_LOG_2_HOST timeout loop that follows a WED SER quiesce trigger
(`docs/WED-breadcrumb-harness-design.md` "Backport retest — NEGATIVE
result"). This is the next candidate the SER patch re-audit flagged
("take only if 03+13 don't resolve the MCU-death loop," now the case):
double-allocating/re-zeroing ring state across repeated
mtk_wed_start()/reset cycles (exactly what mt7915_mac_full_reset()'s
10x retry loop does) could leave WDMA ring state inconsistent with
what the MCU firmware expects on the Nth retry.

No v1/v3 adaptation needed — the touched functions
(mtk_wed_wdma_rx_ring_setup, mtk_wed_wdma_tx_ring_setup,
mtk_wed_tx_ring_setup, mtk_wed_rx_ring_setup, mtk_wed_start) are
version-generic; verified the pre-image matches this tree exactly
(this region is untouched by wed-ser-01/-02). Diff regenerated against
this tree (line numbers differ from the SDK original due to our other
local patches elsewhere in the file); hunk content is unmodified from
upstream (verified with a real patch/compile round-trip, not
hand-transcribed).

